535":"except","H8147":"two","H3871":"tablet","H4872":"Moses","H2722":"Horeb","H3772":"cut","H5973":"with","H3318":"come","H4714":"Egypt","H3588":"for","H4672":"to find","H6942":"consecate","H8104":"obey","H4256":"division","H7891":"to sing","H623":"Asaph","H1968":"Heman","H3038":"Jeduthun","H251":"male-sibling","H3847":"to clothe","H948":"fine linen","H4700":"cymbal","H5035":"bag","H3658":"lyre","H5975":"stand","H4217":"East (Gate)","H4196":"altar","H3967":"hundred","H6242":"twenty","H2690":"to blow","H2689":"trumpet","H259":"one","H8085":"hear","H6963":"voice","H1984":"to shine","H3034":"to give thanks","H7311":"to exalt","H7892":"song","H2896":"pleasant","H5769":"enduring","H2617":"kindness","H4390":"to fill","H6051":"cloud","H3201":"be able","H8334":"to minister","H3519":"glory"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","God, under the care of Selemith. See 1 Paralipomenon xxvi. 26. (Calmet)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Ark. Another was not made, as that was most sacred and excellent. (Worthington)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Day, the eighth, 3 Kings viii. 2."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Levites, with the priests alternately; (3 Kings viii. 2.) or the latter were all Levites, (Calmet) though higher in dignity, in the same manner as our bishops are priests."],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","With the. “And” is omitted in Hebrew but supplied by Protestants, &c., from 3 Kings. (Haydock)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Oracle, pushing out the veil, (Haydock) in the tabernacle of Moses, but not in the temple, which was of larger dimensions. (Calmet) — But if. Hebrew, “but they were not seen without. And there it is till this day.”"],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","Ark. See 3 Kings viii. 9. (Haydock) — The other things which had been placed in, or at least on the side of the ark, were now removed to the treasury rooms. (Tirinus)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Sanctified; free from all legal impediments to offer sacrifice. (Haydock) — Divided. Hebrew, “observed.” (Tirinus) — Protestants, “and they did not then wait by course,” which was the case also with the singers, &c., on this solemn occasion; as the number regulated by David for each week, would not have been sufficient. (Haydock) — The regulation had not yet been reduced to practice. (Menochius) (Calmet) — As yet (Du Hamel) at that time, is omitted (Haydock) by the Septuagint (Du Hamel) and Hebrew."],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Linen, or “robes of silk.” Protestants, “white linen.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Cloud. See 3 Kings viii. 10. (Menochius) — It is called the glory of the Lord, because its appearance was luminous and awful, being a symbol of the divine presence. (Haydock)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}